📧 Maily Detector

A Chrome extension that scans the email you have open in Gmail and uses an AI model to classify it as SPAM, NOT SPAM, or SUBSCRIPTION.

Features
One-click scan of the currently open Gmail email (subject + body)
Classifies emails into three categories, each with its own color:
🟢 NOT SPAM – looks like a legitimate message
🔴 SPAM – shows patterns common in spam or phishing
🔵 SUBSCRIPTION – a subscription or newsletter email, with steps for cancelling
Shows a confidence percentage and the reason for the result
Warns you when an email is mostly Thai, since the model was trained on English only, and lets you scan anyway
How it works
content.js runs inside Gmail and reads the subject and body of the open email (trimmed to 2,000 characters).
When you click Scan, popup.js sends that text to a text-classification model hosted on a Hugging Face Space through the Gradio API.
The result is parsed and shown in the popup with the label, confidence bar and explanation.

The model itself is hosted separately on Hugging Face and is not part of this repository.

Tech stack
Chrome Extension (Manifest V3)
JavaScript, HTML, CSS
Hugging Face Spaces + Gradio API for the AI model
Project structure
maily-detector/
├── manifest.json   # Extension config and permissions
├── content.js      # Reads the open email from the Gmail page
├── popup.html      # Popup UI
└── popup.js        # Calls the AI model and displays the result
Installation
Download or clone this repository.
Open Chrome and go to chrome://extensions.
Turn on Developer mode (top right).
Click Load unpacked and select the maily-detector folder.
Pin the extension from the puzzle-piece icon in the toolbar.
Usage
Open Gmail and click on an email to open it.
Click the Maily Detector icon in the toolbar.
Press Scan and wait for the result.

If you get an error, refresh the Gmail tab and try again. The Hugging Face Space may also need a moment to wake up if it hasn't been used for a while.

Privacy note

The text of the email you scan is sent to the Hugging Face Space for classification. Emails are only read when you press Scan, never in the background.

Limitations
Works with English emails; results on Thai or other languages may be inaccurate.
Depends on Gmail's page structure, so a Gmail layout change could stop it from reading emails.
Requires the Hugging Face Space to be online.
